    {
        "user": "U081Z9041A5",
        "type": "message",
        "ts": "1789053511.276439",
        "client_msg_id": "61df9cca-db26-4bf9-92b1-98de932c8f45",
        "text": "At this stage you do not need either.  You could fork, or you could also just fetch a tar.gz and expand it locally.  For now you most likely will just do 'make; make install' locally.  (At least that's how I work... other modes are of course entirely possible.)   There are also Docker containers like rocker\/drd that already have R-devel and hence have all that is needed to (re-)compile r-devel.",
        "team": "T01DW9DLB2A",
        "user_team": "T01DW9DLB2A",
        "source_team": "T01DW9DLB2A",
        "user_profile": {
            "avatar_hash": "g4e96ca7ae02",
            "image_72": "https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/4e96ca7ae02c37e7d940d17997d780e5.jpg?s=72&d=https%3A%2F%2Fa.slack-edge.com%2Fdf10d%2Fimg%2Favatars%2Fava_0023-72.png",
            "first_name": "Dirk",
            "real_name": "Dirk Eddelbuettel",
            "display_name": "Dirk Eddelbuettel",
            "team": "T01DW9DLB2A",
            "name": "edd",
            "is_restricted": false,
            "is_ultra_restricted": false
        },
        "thread_ts": "1788992168.013759",
        "parent_user_id": "U0C1HLXQX4Y",
        "blocks": [
            {
                "type": "rich_text",
                "block_id": "U1HZs",
                "elements": [
                    {
                        "type": "rich_text_section",
                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "At this stage you do not need either.  You could fork, or you could also just fetch a tar.gz and expand it locally.  For now you most likely will just do 'make; make install' locally.  (At least that's how I work... other modes are of course entirely possible.)   There are also Docker containers like rocker\/drd that already have R-devel and hence have all that is needed to (re-)compile r-devel."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "user": "U081Z9041A5",
        "type": "message",
        "ts": "1789053678.593619",
        "client_msg_id": "478ab445-5d0c-4bd2-8cab-b96263238fed",
        "text": "In fact, as you are essentially working on one function you could also rely on just `R CMD SHLIB ...` and all that jazz (or do `Rcpp::sourceCpp()` which wraps it).  No need to fully rebuild all of R.  Different approaches are possible, I am not sure what the 'recommended' one is.",
        "team": "T01DW9DLB2A",
        "user_team": "T01DW9DLB2A",
        "source_team": "T01DW9DLB2A",
        "user_profile": {
            "avatar_hash": "g4e96ca7ae02",
            "image_72": "https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/4e96ca7ae02c37e7d940d17997d780e5.jpg?s=72&d=https%3A%2F%2Fa.slack-edge.com%2Fdf10d%2Fimg%2Favatars%2Fava_0023-72.png",
            "first_name": "Dirk",
            "real_name": "Dirk Eddelbuettel",
            "display_name": "Dirk Eddelbuettel",
            "team": "T01DW9DLB2A",
            "name": "edd",
            "is_restricted": false,
            "is_ultra_restricted": false
        },
        "thread_ts": "1788992168.013759",
        "parent_user_id": "U0C1HLXQX4Y",
        "blocks": [
            {
                "type": "rich_text",
                "block_id": "URFtl",
                "elements": [
                    {
                        "type": "rich_text_section",
                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "In fact, as you are essentially working on one function you could also rely on just "
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "R CMD SHLIB ...",
                                "style": {
                                    "code": true
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": " and all that jazz (or do "
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "Rcpp::sourceCpp()",
                                "style": {
                                    "code": true
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": " which wraps it).  No need to fully rebuild all of R.  Different approaches are possible, I am not sure what the 'recommended' one is."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "text": "I fiddled around with some documentation <https:\/\/contributor.r-project.org\/rdevguide\/chapters\/lifecycle_of_a_patch.html|on this guide> and was able to get the svn trunk and build a minimal version with the C implementation. The minimal patch is attached.\n\nI was able to run the above example on my local version of R getting the following results:\n\n```bench::mark(small = {attr(y, \"foo\") &lt;- z; attr(y, \"foo\") &lt;- \"\"}, large = {attr(y, \"foo\") &lt;- lst; attr(y, \"foo\") &lt;- \"\"})\n# A tibble: 2 × 13\n  expression      min   median  `itr\/sec` mem_alloc `gc\/sec` n_itr  n_gc\n  &lt;bch:expr&gt; &lt;bch:tm&gt; &lt;bch:tm&gt;      &lt;dbl&gt; &lt;bch:byt&gt;    &lt;dbl&gt; &lt;int&gt; &lt;dbl&gt;\n1 small      861.01ns 943.08ns 458313.           0B        0 10000     0\n2 large         6.62s    6.62s      0.151        0B        0     1     0```\nAnd then with the following patch:\n\n```bench::mark(small = {attr(y, \"foo\") &lt;- z; attr(y, \"foo\") &lt;- \"\"}, large = {attr(y, \"foo\") &lt;- lst; attr(y, \"foo\") &lt;- \"\"})\n# A tibble: 2 × 13\n  expression     min  median `itr\/sec` mem_alloc `gc\/sec` n_itr  n_gc \n  &lt;bch:expr&gt; &lt;bch:t&gt; &lt;bch:t&gt;     &lt;dbl&gt; &lt;bch:byt&gt;    &lt;dbl&gt; &lt;int&gt; &lt;dbl&gt; \n1 small       1.02µs  1.93µs  475970.         NA     47.6  9999     1  \n2 large      27.38ms 34.22ms      29.2        NA     25.1     7     6  ```\nWhere `z` is just a simple vector and simulates the cost of building the hashmap anytime `R_fixupRHS` is called.",
