                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "I fiddled around with some documentation "
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "link",
                                "url": "https:\/\/contributor.r-project.org\/rdevguide\/chapters\/lifecycle_of_a_patch.html",
                                "text": "on this guide"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": " and was able to get the svn trunk and build a minimal version with the C implementation. The minimal patch is attached.\n\nI was able to run the above example on my local version of R getting the following results:\n\n"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "rich_text_preformatted",
                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "bench::mark(small = {attr(y, \"foo\") <- z; attr(y, \"foo\") <- \"\"}, large = {attr(y, \"foo\") <- lst; attr(y, \"foo\") <- \"\"})\n# A tibble: 2 × 13\n  expression      min   median  `itr\/sec` mem_alloc `gc\/sec` n_itr  n_gc\n  <bch:expr> <bch:tm> <bch:tm>      <dbl> <bch:byt>    <dbl> <int> <dbl>\n1 small      861.01ns 943.08ns 458313.           0B        0 10000     0\n2 large         6.62s    6.62s      0.151        0B        0     1     0"
                            }
                        ],
                        "border": 0
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "rich_text_section",
                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "\nAnd then with the following patch:\n\n"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "rich_text_preformatted",
                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "bench::mark(small = {attr(y, \"foo\") <- z; attr(y, \"foo\") <- \"\"}, large = {attr(y, \"foo\") <- lst; attr(y, \"foo\") <- \"\"})\n# A tibble: 2 × 13\n  expression     min  median `itr\/sec` mem_alloc `gc\/sec` n_itr  n_gc \n  <bch:expr> <bch:t> <bch:t>     <dbl> <bch:byt>    <dbl> <int> <dbl> \n1 small       1.02µs  1.93µs  475970.         NA     47.6  9999     1  \n2 large      27.38ms 34.22ms      29.2        NA     25.1     7     6  "
                            }
                        ],
                        "border": 0
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "rich_text_section",
                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "\nWhere "
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "z",
                                "style": {
                                    "code": true
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": " is just a simple vector and simulates the cost of building the hashmap anytime "
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "R_fixupRHS",
                                "style": {
                                    "code": true
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": " is called."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            }
        ],
