                        "type": "rich_text_section",
                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "That is the final step. Bugzilla emails go to all R Core member AFAIK. But yes, one-off initial cost of getting a handle to submit (because spammers...)\n\nAlternatively, you could set up a quick GH repo for the patch, or fork the r-devel repo at GH, and comment on your PR, changes and results in a markdown document (or gist).  And then email the r-devel list to get in front of the same crowd."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ]
